---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout page="about" prompt="cat about.md">
  <!-- #attn-root marks the region tokenized for the attention overlay.
       scripts/precompute_attention.py wraps every token here in a .tok span. -->
  <main id="attn-root">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="page-title">Zirui Ren (任梓瑞)</h1>
      <div class="page-sub">Beijing, China</div>
      <p>
        I am currently a senior at the Department of Physics, Tsinghua
        University, and an incoming PhD at the College of AI, Tsinghua University.
        I am currently working with
        <a href="https://kindxiaoming.github.io/">Prof. Ziming Liu</a>
        on AI4AI. Previously, I have also collaborated with
        <a href="https://nlp.csai.tsinghua.edu.cn/~lzy/">Prof. Zhiyuan Liu</a>
        and researchers at ModelBest (面壁智能) on long-context foundation models.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am excited about enabling frontier models to conduct innovative research,
        both on natural science (AI for Science) and on their own training (AI for AI, a.k.a. RSI).
        The paths I explored cover data synthesis, benchmarking and agentic systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        For this, I do adopt the top-down approach, e.g., black-box tuning on a strong pretrained model.
        Besides, I also take the bottom-up approach, prioritizing understanding over benchmark scores (a.k.a. Physics/Science of AI).
        This approach comprises mechanistic interpretability, training dynamics and optimization theory.
        My personal (and perhaps dissensual) belief is that bottom-up insights shall be the evergreen intellectual legacies of human research.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="blk">
      <h2 class="sec-title">Education</h2>
      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-title">Tsinghua University, Beijing</div>
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="date">2023 — present</span> · Physics major ·
          GPA 3.93/4.0
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Selected Awards:</strong> Tsinghua Comprehensive Excellence
            Scholarship (Top 5%, 2024 &amp; 2025)
          </li>
          <li><strong>Language:</strong> TOEFL 113/120 · CET-6 665/710</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <h2 class="sec-title">Research &amp; Internship Experience</h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-title">
          ArchitectureIQ: Benchmarking Deep Learning Modeling Intuition
        </div>
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="date">2026.06 — present</span> · Advisor: Prof. Ziming
          Liu, College of AI, Tsinghua Univ.
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            In high-level abstraction, self-evolving AI is essentially optimization in the configuration space.
            Agentic frameworks handle the high-level feedback loop well.
            However, local adjustments, like tuning a parameter or tweaking the architecture, are highly under-optimized.
            We believe that before being able to propose better settings,
            the agent should (at least) have intuitions on what a good one look like.
            We are developing <a href="https://github.com/renrua52/ArchitectureIQ">ArchitectureIQ</a>,
            a benchmark gauging exactly this capability.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-title">
          OPHIS: Towards Mechanistic Auto-Research
        </div>
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="date">2026.06 — present</span> · Advisor: Prof. Ziming
          Liu, College of AI, Tsinghua Univ.
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Today's auto-research systems mostly do trial-and-error: 
            they remix Internet priors or remember what worked before, 
            but rarely explain <strong>why</strong>. 
            We propose mechanistic auto-research via OPHIS — 
            Observation → Problem → Hypothesis → Intervention → Speed-up — 
            a pipeline that turns insight about internal training dynamics into practical speedup tricks.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-title">
          Mechanistic Analysis of Reasoning Models
        </div>
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="date">2025.07 — 2026.03</span> · Collaboration with MIT ·
          Advisor: Dr. Ziming Liu
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            I conducted a systematic mechanistic study on Hierarchical Reasoning Models (HRMs). 
            By probing latent-state trajectories and structural
            geometry, I identified critical violations of fixed-point
            assumptions, proving that advanced reasoners exhibit a hidden "guessing" shortcut.
            Inspired by this insight, I engineered 3 training-free,
            boosting accuracy on <em>Sudoku-Extreme</em> from 55% to <strong>97%</strong>.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-title">
          Research Intern, Long-Context Foundation Models
        </div>
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="date">2025.06 — 2025.08</span> · ModelBest Inc.
          (面壁智能) · Advisor: Prof. Zhiyuan Liu
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            As an early-stage collaborator exploring sub-quadratic MiniCPM model architectures,
            I conducted fine-grained ablation studies on linear/sparse attention modules, laying the empirical
            foundation for ModelBest's million-context <strong>SALA-9B</strong> model.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-title">
          Research Intern, Test-Time Scaling for Long-to-long Generation
        </div>
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="date">2025.02 — 2025.08</span> · ModelBest Inc.
          (面壁智能) · Advisor: Prof. Zhiyuan Liu
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            I co-developed LLM×MapReduce-V2, a test-time scaling framework borrowing CNN convolutional
            concepts to map ultra-long contexts into structured graphs for long-to-long generation.
            We scaled the algorithmic prototype into
            <a href="https://surveygo.znyx.com.cn/">SurveyGO</a>, ModelBest's
            production-level academic survey platform, supporting long survey generation from massive references.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="blk">
      <h2 class="sec-title">Publications</h2>

      <div class="pub">
        <div class="pub-title">
          Are Your Reasoning Models Reasoning or Guessing? A Mechanistic
          Analysis of Hierarchical Reasoning Models
        </div>
        <div class="pub-authors"><strong>Zirui Ren</strong>, Ziming Liu</div>
        <div class="pub-venue">
          arXiv:2601.10679 · under review at NeurIPS 2026 (first author)
        </div>
        <img src="/assets/images/hrm.png" alt="HRM analysis figure" />
        <div class="fig-label">
          fig 1. latent-state trajectories of hierarchical reasoners
        </div>
        <p>
          We perform a systematic mechanistic study of hierarchical reasoning
          models. By probing latent-state trajectories and structural geometry,
          we identify critical violations of fixed-point assumptions and a
          hidden "guessing" shortcut in advanced reasoners. We propose three
          training-free augmentation techniques that improve HRM accuracy on
          <em>Sudoku-Extreme</em> from 55% to 97%, and release an
          <a href="https://github.com/renrua52/hrm-mechanistic-analysis"
            >open-source pipeline</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pub">
        <div class="pub-title">
          LLM×MapReduce-V2: Entropy-Driven Convolutional Test-Time Scaling for
          Generating Long-Form Articles from Extremely Long Resources
        </div>
        <div class="pub-authors">
          Haoyu Wang, Yujia Fu, Zhu Zhang, Shuo Wang,
          <strong>Zirui Ren</strong>, Xiaorong Wang, Zhili Li, Chaoqun He, Bo
          An, Zhiyuan Liu, Maosong Sun
        </div>
        <div class="pub-venue">arXiv:2504.05732</div>
        <img
          src="/assets/images/llm_mapreduce.png"
          alt="LLMxMapReduce-V2 figure"
        />
        <div class="fig-label">
          fig 2. convolutional test-time scaling pipeline
        </div>
        <p>
          We develop a test-time scaling framework inspired by convolutional
          architectures, enabling high-fidelity long-form text generation from
          extremely long inputs. The method is deployed in
          <a href="https://surveygo.znyx.com.cn/">SurveyGO</a>, ModelBest's
          production-level academic survey platform.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script src="/js/attention.js" defer></script>
</BaseLayout>
